7592186065136 #edb/ref 1061 18871 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065136 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "213c99f3-2e96-5282-8c9f-7798f6d583ee" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065136 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064257 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065137 #edb/ref 1061 18872 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065137 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "2ca88a28-b372-506f-bc28-472bf491340a" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065137 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186064258 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065367 #edb/ref 1064 "Fractions that contain multiple terms in the numerator and a single term in the denominator can be split into separate terms.\n\nFor example, \n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {x + 2} {3} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac x 3 + \\dfrac 2 3\n\t}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {3a - 4b + 1} {5} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac {3a} 5 - \\dfrac {4b} 5 + \\dfrac 1 5.\n\t}\n$$\n\nOften, we're able to simplify the fractions in the individual terms, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\eqalign{\n\t\t\\dfrac {10x + 9} {2} &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac {10x} {2} + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\\n\t\t\\dfrac {10} {2} \\cdot x + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\\t\n\t\t5 \\cdot x + \\dfrac 9 2 &= \\\n\t\t5x + \\dfrac 9 2 \n\t}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065367 #edb/ref 1065 3375 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065367 #edb/ref 1066 #uuid "0a37b6ec-6750-5aea-ae26-ad82d059a0ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186065367 #edb/ref 1067 "Introduction" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536363 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536461 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536601 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186536623 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186072620 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 1