568 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073885 #edb/ref 1042 #uuid "309e24a1-6c8c-5705-beca-001fed696acc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186074880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1045 "Graphing Ratios" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186074877 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186050948 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1050 420.0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186073979 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "b18f153a-24ae-52c2-833b-f1d51a752952" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074397 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186072620 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074397 #edb/ref 1069 "q-59984" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074397 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074397 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/47/4777b642ae90300bcdcb33e2377067113a78f04a5a891a1c332178619291b6ad.png)\n\nNancy is making lemonade. The amount of water she needs for a given amount of lemon juice is given in the graph above. In its simplest form, what is the ratio of lemon juice to water?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074397 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "57ed4a6f-262c-5ecd-8ab6-efd8ae2df206" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074397 #edb/ref 1074 "One of the points belonging to the graph is $(10,15).$\n\nLet's write the ratio $10:15$ as a fraction:\n\n$$\n\\frac{10}{15}\n$$\n\nWe can simplify this fraction by dividing both the numerator and the denominator by $5$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{10÷5}{15÷5} & =\\frac{2}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the ratio of lemon juice to water is $2:3.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074877 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074878 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074877 #edb/ref 1061 7803 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074877 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e3c01e56-883c-55ab-9e6a-10ceb0575884" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074877 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186074968 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074878 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074879 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074878 #edb/ref 1061 7804 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074878 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5eafd168-51d7-5307-98d8-6cbe0835f715" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074878 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073883 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074879 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186074880 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074879 #edb/ref 1061 7807 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074879 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7b457667-0972-5621-9729-0ef04c05c3b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074879 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073884 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074880 #edb/ref 1061 7809 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074880 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "ca8053f2-49d8-5357-8a87-8e0ac9d72e07" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074880 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186073885 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186074968 #edb/ref 1064 "Remember that we can place equivalent ratios in a ratio table, like the one below.\n\n| $\\color{blue}x$ | $\\color{red}y$ |\n| --- | --- |\n| $\\color{blue}1$ | $\\color{red}2$ |\n| $\\color{blue}2$ | $\\color{red}4$ |\n| $\\color{blue}4$ | $\\color{red}8$ |\n\nBy setting the values in the left column as $\\color{blue}x$-coordinates and the values in the right column as the corresponding $\\color{red}y$-coordinates, we can graph the points to represent a relationship between the ratios.\n\nIn this case, we have the following ordered pairs: $({\\color{blue}1},{\\color{red}2}),$ $({\\color{blue}2},{\\color{red}4}),$ $({\\color{blue}4},{\\color{red}8}).$\n\nPlotting these points on a coordinate plane, we get the following graph:\n\n![](images/0c/0c4abb8d462730ed9b532feeca1e0a800f5376a978bfc799afb